# LibreWolf webgl-prompt-default.patch
#
# Upstream file touched: modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml
#   (the `librewolf.webgl.prompt` entry that patches/webgl-permission-common.patch
#   adds to it — this patch applies AFTER that one, i.e. after common.txt)
#
# What LibreWolf wants instead, and why
# -------------------------------------
# `librewolf.webgl.prompt` defaults to true, which is what makes desktop
# LibreWolf refuse a WebGL context until the user answers a doorhanger. On
# Android that default is not "stricter", it is fatal, and silently so — this is
# landmine L1 in docs/android/AGENTS.md:
#
#   * ClientWebGLContext.cpp's IsWebGLAllowed_impl() fails closed for every
#     principal that has no explicit "webgl" permission, and asks the parent to
#     prompt;
#   * BrowserParent::RecvShowWebGLPermissionPrompt() early-returns because
#     `mFrameElement->AsBrowser()` yields nothing — GeckoView has no XUL
#     <browser>;
#   * the "webgl-permissions-prompt" observers, the doorhanger markup, the icons
#     and WebGLPermissionPromptHelper.sys.mjs all live under browser/, which an
#     Android build never contains (they are in
#     patches/webgl-permission-desktop.patch, a desktop.txt entry).
#
# So on Android nothing can ever grant the permission and every WebGL context
# fails — with no crash, no console error and no visible prompt. "It installs and
# it browses" still passes. Hence: false on Android, true everywhere else, and it
# ships in the same change as the split, never as a follow-up.
#
# Why this is a separate Android patch and not a hunk in the common half
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# patches/android/README.md says shared-Gecko changes belong in one common patch
# with the Android behaviour gated in-tree, and the resulting tree here does
# exactly that — the gate is the `#if defined(ANDROID)` below. Only the delivery
# is split out, because LW-M1-08 requires the desktop tree after
# common+desktop to stay byte-identical to the tree the old single
# webgl-permission.patch produced. Putting the #if in the common half would
# change modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml on desktop too, which breaks
# that. assets/patches/android.txt has named this file's job since LW-M1-01
# ("the librewolf.webgl.prompt default that landmine L1 requires").
#
# The README's drift hazard does not apply: the context below is LibreWolf's own
# pref block, not upstream text, so if webgl-permission-common.patch ever stops
# applying this patch rejects loudly too rather than applying against something
# it did not mean.
#
# Ordering (load-bearing)
# -----------------------
# Requires patches/webgl-permission-common.patch to have been applied first.
# assets/patches/common.txt is always applied before android.txt, so listing this
# in android.txt is enough.
#
# Nothing happens outside this diff (landmine L4): no file copies, no rm, no
# generated file is edited by hand. The value reaches the binary through
# modules/libpref/init/generate_static_pref_list.py, which preprocesses this yaml
# with buildconfig.defines["ALLDEFINES"]; ANDROID is in there via
# build/moz.configure/init.configure:924 `set_define("ANDROID", target_is_android)`.
#
--- a/modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml
+++ b/modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml
@@ -11824,9 +11824,21 @@
 # Prefs starting with "librewolf."
 #---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 
+# LibreWolf for Android (LW-M1-08, landmine L1): this must default to false on
+# Android. The prompt has no UI there - the doorhanger, its observers and
+# WebGLPermissionPromptHelper.sys.mjs all live under browser/, which an Android
+# build never contains, and BrowserParent::RecvShowWebGLPermissionPrompt returns
+# early because GeckoView has no XUL <browser> to notify. With the desktop
+# default of true, IsWebGLAllowed_impl fails closed for every origin that has no
+# explicit "webgl" permission and nothing can ever grant one, so every WebGL
+# context dies with no crash and no console error. Desktop keeps true.
 - name: librewolf.webgl.prompt
   type: RelaxedAtomicBool
+#if defined(ANDROID)
+  value: false
+#else
   value: true
+#endif
   mirror: always
 
 - name: librewolf.webgl.prompt.hide
